/target_source.rs","fingerprint":"finding-0d9e741858db75be08e2b837ca598acc","last_repair_wave_id":"repair-wave-df745a3cb80981aca4e2be1bc91519a2","max_repair_attempts":2,"owner_task_id":"002","repair_attempts":1,"review_cycle_id":"review-cycle-0","root_cause_status":"confirmed","scope":"admitted","status":"in-progress","updated_at":"2026-09-19T17:53:18.328Z","violated_invariant":"Thread request control through boundary discovery and check cancellation/deadline within the backward scan so planning and boundary I/O terminate promptly, with a test that changes control state during the scan rather than only before the request."},{"admitted_at":"2026-09-19T17:29:30.461Z","category":"persistent-test-oracle","decision":"mechanical","evidence_refs":["native/codex-rollout-collector/tests/rollout_blockers.rs","native/codex-rollout-collector/tests/stage4_target_protocol.rs","docs/codex/codex-rollout-collector-architecture.md","docs/workflow/CURRENT_TASK.md","docs/codex/codex-rollout-isolated-closure-verification.md","docs/changes/records/CR-20260916-rollout-blockers-s1.md"],"failure_condition":"The newly admitted P-12 test only checks non-empty tool details, turn IDs, and keys, does not prove a tool begin/end straddles windows or that logical keys remain equal across overlap/retry, and explicitly asserts that known_complete_range rereads 0..known.end, locking in the range-progression defect.","file":"native/codex-rollout-collector/tests/rollout_blockers.rs","fingerprint":"finding-f055a9eb19e6da4e496a31f4bea6b66a","last_repair_wave_id":"repair-wave-df745a3cb80981aca4e2be1bc91519a2","max_repair_attempts":2,"owner_task_id":"002","repair_attempts":1,"review_cycle_id":"review-cycle-0","root_cause_status":"confirmed","scope":"admitted","status":"in-progress","updated_at":"2026-09-19T17:53:18.944Z","violated_invariant":"Use independently specified assertions for exact cross-window tool association, key equality across reread/overlap, correct missing-range progression to terminal cover